  "body": "Consider this IDL:\n\n```\n[SecureContext]\ninterface A {};\n[NoInterfaceObject]\ninterface B {\n  void foo();\n}\nA implements B;\n```\n\nIs the `foo` method available on `A` objects in non-secure contexts?  Per the current spec text, I'm pretty sure it is, right?  That's probably OK, but may be worth an example in the spec.\n\n@mikewest \n",
